  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Ellingham diagram is graph of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;G</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></math> vs <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math> of any metal/element oxide. since</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;G</mi><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>&#916;H</mi><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>T&#916;S</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p><p>for most metal oxide formation&nbsp;metal (s) + oxygen (g) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8594;</mo></math>metal oxide (s)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>ve</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;S</mi><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>ve</mi></math></p><p>so graph will be a straight line with - ve y-intracept &amp; + ve slope.</p>",
